  "section_notes": "The final S2 has no sales stop, no transition limit, and a permanent 5% cap that only triggers corrective action and regulator review, which largely protects Northwind's Hearth 10 at 6.2%. The S5 recall trigger of 8 per 100,000 is mandatory with no interim allowance, which exposes Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9, although recall is explicitly not a permanent ban. Per-model results go to purchasers and regulators but not to the public, and the 6-year retrofit and 36-month suppression deadlines sit inside the acceptable ranges."
